   "whatAmILookingAt": "Two bars, each one whole cut into four equal quarters, over a number line from 0 to 2. The slider counts quarters from the left: the counted ones shade in, filling the first bar and then the second, and the mark on the line sits where the shading ends. Each quarter moves the mark a quarter along, so place = count ÷ 4: 3 gives 0.75 (3/4), 7 gives 1.75 (7/4 = 1 3/4). The readouts split the count into whole bars filled and quarters past them.",
